# Sensitive-data patterns for pr-reviewer.
#
# Copy this file to ~/.config/pr-reviewer/sensitive-patterns (or point
# PRREVIEW_SENSITIVE_PATTERNS_FILE at your copy) and add what is secret in YOUR
# environment: internal hostnames, private IP ranges, customer names.
#
# One extended regular expression (grep -E) per line, matched case-insensitively.
# Lines starting with # and blank lines are ignored.
#
# Every comment the reviewer is about to post is checked against this list,
# and so are the title and description of every PR it reviews, and the title
# and body of the issue the PR links. A hit in an outgoing comment, or a scan
# that cannot run, means that comment is not posted. A hit in a PR's title,
# description or linked issue means that PR is not reviewed.
# The reviewer refuses to start without this file.

# Private keys
-----BEGIN [A-Z ]*PRIVATE KEY-----
# AWS access key id
AKIA[0-9A-Z]{16}
# GitHub tokens
gh[pousr]_[A-Za-z0-9]{36}
github_pat_[A-Za-z0-9_]{22,}
# Anthropic and OpenAI API keys
sk-ant-[A-Za-z0-9_-]{20,}
sk-(proj-)?[A-Za-z0-9]{32,}
# Slack tokens
xox[abposr]-[A-Za-z0-9-]{10,}
# Google API key
AIza[0-9A-Za-z_-]{35}
